{"id":"chatcmpl-fe87da56-bd9f-45f8-bcfe-c55398c72dd5","object":"chat.completion","created":1795250139,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"{\n  \"highlights\": \"The task required identifying a subtle finding (abdominal calcinosis) and its laterality in a chest X-ray, where initial model queries failed due to low sensitivity. Success came from systematically escalating: querying multiple models, then using localization tools, and finally zooming into the region of interest to visually confirm the finding and laterality. The key was combining model outputs with targeted visual inspection when models were unreliable.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When multiple models fail to detect a finding, escalate to region-of-interest cropping and zooming for direct visual inspection.\",\n    \"For laterality questions, always confirm using radiological convention (patient's left = viewer's right) after localizing the finding.\",\n    \"Use phrase grounding or grounded report tools to attempt localization before manual cropping, but be prepared to override if they miss subtle findings.\",\n    \"Cross-check findings with at least two independent models to assess reliability; if they disagree or miss, rely on visual inspection of the cropped region.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical Imaging Analysis\": \"Start with multiple model queries for detection and laterality; if inconsistent or negative, use localization tools and then crop/zoom to the relevant anatomical region for visual confirmation.\",\n    \"Visual Question Answering with Subtle Findings\": \"When findings are subtle, models may have low sensitivity; always include a step to zoom into the suspected area and inspect visually, using radiological conventions for orientation.\",\n    \"Tool Orchestration for Diagnosis\": \"Chain tools from general to specific: first ask models, then use grounding/localization, then crop and re-ask or visually inspect; document reasoning at each step.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm laterality using radiological convention: patient's left is on the viewer's right in frontal views.\",\n    \"When models miss a finding, crop the region of interest and zoom in to visually verify presence and location.\"\n  ]\n}"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":708,"total_tokens":1106,"completion_tokens":398,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":708},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":398}}}